                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/1534: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-01T19:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1940—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>128. Department’s 122, June 22, 1940. Mr. Harry Hawkins, Chief of the Division of
                    Commercial Treaties and Agreements, and Mr. George Luthringer of the Office of
                    the Economic Adviser, have been selected for the mission. Please ascertain and
                    inform the Department when these officers should arrive in Argentina.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
